{"path":"numeric/complex/acos","title":"std::acos(std::complex)","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>acos<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">(std::complex)</span>","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/numeric/complex/acos","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"Computes complex arc cosine of a complex value z. Branch cuts exist outside the interval [−1, +1] along the real axis.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/complex\">&lt;complex&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <br>complex<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> acos<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> complex<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> z <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Computes complex arc cosine of a complex value <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code>. Branch cuts exist outside the interval <span class=\"texhtml\">[−1, +1]</span> along the real axis.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> z\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> complex value\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>If no errors occur, complex arc cosine of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is returned, in the range of a strip unbounded along the imaginary axis and in the interval <span class=\"texhtml\">[0, +π]</span> along the real axis.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Error_handling_and_special_values\">Error handling and special values</h3>\n<p>Errors are reported consistent with <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/math_errhandling\">math_errhandling</a></span>.\n</p><p>If the implementation supports IEEE floating-point arithmetic,\n</p>\n<ul><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/acos\"><span class=\"kw1345\">std::<span class=\"me2\">acos</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/conj\"><span class=\"kw2708\">std::<span class=\"me2\">conj</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/conj\"><span class=\"kw2708\">std::<span class=\"me2\">conj</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/acos\"><span class=\"kw1345\">std::<span class=\"me2\">acos</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(±0,+0)</code>, the result is <code>(π/2,-0)</code>\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(±0,NaN)</code>, the result is <code>(π/2,NaN)</code>\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(x,+∞)</code> (for any finite x), the result is <code>(π/2,-∞)</code>\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(x,NaN)</code> (for any nonzero finite x), the result is <code>(NaN,NaN)</code> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/fenv/FE_exceptions\">FE_INVALID</a></span> may be raised.\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(-∞,y)</code> (for any positive finite y), the result is <code>(π,-∞)</code>\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(+∞,y)</code> (for any positive finite y), the result is <code>(+0,-∞)</code>\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(-∞,+∞)</code>, the result is <code>(3π/4,-∞)</code>\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(+∞,+∞)</code>, the result is <code>(π/4,-∞)</code>\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(±∞,NaN)</code>, the result is <code>(NaN,±∞)</code> (the sign of the imaginary part is unspecified)\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(NaN,y)</code> (for any finite y), the result is <code>(NaN,NaN)</code> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/fenv/FE_exceptions\">FE_INVALID</a></span> may be raised\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(NaN,+∞)</code>, the result is <code>(NaN,-∞)</code>\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(NaN,NaN)</code>, the result is <code>(NaN,NaN)</code>\n</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Inverse cosine (or arc cosine) is a multivalued function and requires a branch cut on the complex plane. The branch cut is conventionally placed at the line segments <span class=\"texhtml\">(-∞,-1)</span> and <span class=\"texhtml\">(1,∞)</span> of the real axis.\n</p>\nThe mathematical definition of the principal value of arc cosine is <span class=\"texhtml\">acos z = <span class=\"t-mfrac\"><table><tr><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td></tr></table></span>π + <i>i</i>ln(<i>i</i>z + <span class=\"t-mrad\"><span>√</span><span>1-z<span class=\"t-su\">2<br></span></span></span>)</span>.\n<p>For any <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code>, <span class=\"texhtml\">acos(z) = π - acos(-z)</span>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cmath&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;complex&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/manip/fixed\"><span class=\"kw1801\">std::<span class=\"me2\">fixed</span></span></a><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> z1<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu16\">2.0</span>, <span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"acos\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> z1 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/acos\"><span class=\"kw1345\">std::<span class=\"me2\">acos</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z1<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> z2<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu16\">2.0</span>, <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"acos\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> z2 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" (the other side of the cut) = \"</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/acos\"><span class=\"kw1345\">std::<span class=\"me2\">acos</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z2<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// for any z, acos(z) = pi - acos(-z)</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> pi <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/acos\"><span class=\"kw1345\">std::<span class=\"me2\">acos</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> z3 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> pi <span class=\"sy2\">-</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/acos\"><span class=\"kw1345\">std::<span class=\"me2\">acos</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z2<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"cos(pi - acos\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> z2 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\") = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/cos\"><span class=\"kw1342\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cos</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z3<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>acos(-2.000000,0.000000) = (3.141593,-1.316958)\nacos(-2.000000,-0.000000) (the other side of the cut) = (3.141593,1.316958)\ncos(pi - acos(-2.000000,-0.000000)) = (2.000000,0.000000)</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/asin\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>asin<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::complex)</span></span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes arc sine of a complex number (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\arcsin{z}}\">arcsin(z)</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/atan\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>atan<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::complex)</span></span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes arc tangent of a complex number (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\arctan{z}}\">arctan(z)</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/cos\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>cos<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::complex)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes cosine of a complex number (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\cos{z}}\">cos(z)</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/acos\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>acos</span><span>acosf</span><span>acosl</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes arc cosine (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\arccos{x}}\">arccos(x)</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/acos\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>acos<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::valarray)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  applies the function <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/acos\">std::acos</a></span> to each element of valarray <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/cacos\">C documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>cacos</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Error handling and special values","id":"Error_handling_and_special_values"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics library"},{"path":"numeric/complex","title":"std::complex"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::acos(std::complex)","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++11. Computes complex arc cosine of a complex value z. Branch cuts exist outside the interval [−1, +1] along the real axis."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"z"},{"label":"Return value","note":"If no errors occur, complex arc cosine of z is returned, in the range of a strip unbounded along the imaginary axis and in the interval [0, +π] along the real…"},{"label":"Error handling and special values","note":"Errors are reported consistent with math_errhandling."},{"label":"Notes","note":"Inverse cosine (or arc cosine) is a multivalued function and requires a branch cut on the complex plane."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"asin(std::complex)","note":"computes arc sine of a complex number (arcsin(z))"},{"label":"atan(std::complex)","note":"computes arc tangent of a complex number (arctan(z))"},{"label":"cos(std::complex)","note":"computes cosine of a complex number (cos(z))"},{"label":"acos, acosf, acosl","note":"computes arc cosine (arccos(x))"},{"label":"acos(std::valarray)","note":"applies the function std::acos to each element of valarray"}]}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":458,"codeBlockCount":2}
